    <p class="govuk-!-margin-bottom-2">
On 19 August 2024 at approximately 7:40 PM, a man and a woman entered Quibblesworth Fine Jewellers in Little Puddington, posing as customers. The man, tall with a muscular build, asked about Rolex watches, while the woman, slim with brown hair, appeared nervous and held a hammer. Shortly after, the man vaulted the counter and assaulted the shop owner, Mr. Quibblesworth, demanding he open the safe. The woman threatened employee Ms. Plinkerton with the hammer, forcing her to the floor.
</p>

    <p class="govuk-!-margin-bottom-2">
The man struck Mr. Quibblesworth multiple times and emptied the safe of valuable items worth approximately £127,000. Meanwhile, the woman smashed glass display cases and filled a large bag with jewellery. At around 7:47 PM, both suspects fled the shop and entered a dark blue saloon car parked nearby, with the woman driving. A passerby, Mr. Fizzlebottom, called emergency services, and police arrived within 8 minutes. Mr. Quibblesworth sustained a fractured wrist, a concussion, and head injuries. Both employees suffered psychological trauma.    </p>
